  "question": "Do direct no-OCR C-II-N crossings from 49 through 58 continue the whole-integer threshold pattern, and does an explicit Shoushi/Datong qi-ce accumulated coordinate replay the complete postdated 1624 stepped transition sequence without falsely proving a pre-1578 parent or a unique day-counting convention?",
  "answer": "YES FOR A SEVENTEEN-THRESHOLD INTERIOR MECHANICAL SERIES AND STRONG POSTDATED OFFSET COMPATIBILITY; NO FOR A UNIVERSAL FLOOR RULE, A UNIQUE COUNTING CONVENTION, OR THE EXACT PRE-1578 SANMING/YUELING PARENT. Direct visual re-collation closes 49..58 crossings at d81/82, d88/89, d96/97, d104/105, d111/112, d119/120, d127/128, d136/137, d146/147 and d160/161. Combined with Batch 12DO, every integer 42..58 is crossed by adjacent C-II-N days. A third forward-only correction places 2494.04 at d88 rather than the exploratory 12CG d89, with exact d89=2500.61. Received Shoushi qi-ce is 15.2184375 days and cumulative solar-term coordinates align every 1624 received transition from 42 through 58 to its C-II-N first-crossing day within about 0.5291 day when elapsed-day and ordinal-day readings are both retained as philological candidates. The 1624 witness is postdated, the count convention is not selected, and the C-II-N summer maximum remains 58.6332 rather than 59, so chronology and endpoint firewalls remain active.",
